# #72 #73: /ttl reset is a full character reset (life/soul_wipe.js). Expect no "ttl:" failure lines.
# A Life 2 Slime with a common skill, a resistance, an extra skill and 50,000 max magicule comes back to Life 1 as a
# fresh Human: none of those abilities, Human's own EP (max magicule 50-70), race Human. Then a Life 1 death takes the
# abilities the Human body learned in Life 1 (here a granted resistance) before the Corridor.
ttlbot spawn TtlBotWipe
@sleep 4
kill TtlBotWipe
execute as TtlBotWipe run ttl wish knowledge
execute as TtlBotWipe run ttl choose slime
@sleep 2
tensura edit ability grant TtlBotWipe tensura:telepathy
tensura edit ability grant TtlBotWipe tensura:cold_resistance
tensura edit ability grant TtlBotWipe tensura:magic_sense
tensura edit stat TtlBotWipe magicule max set 50000
ttl wipe TtlBotWipe expect has tensura:telepathy yes
ttl wipe TtlBotWipe expect has tensura:cold_resistance yes
ttl wipe TtlBotWipe expect has tensura:magic_sense yes
ttl wipe TtlBotWipe
ttl reset TtlBotWipe
@sleep 2
ttl wipe TtlBotWipe
ttl wipe TtlBotWipe expect has tensura:telepathy no
ttl wipe TtlBotWipe expect has tensura:cold_resistance no
ttl wipe TtlBotWipe expect has tensura:magic_sense no
ttl wipe TtlBotWipe expect count 0
# Tensura never forgets a resistance: it drops back to the start of learning (negative mastery), which is not held.
ttl wipe TtlBotWipe expect magicule 70
ttl racelock TtlBotWipe expect tensura:human
ttl karma TtlBotWipe expect phase life1
# The Life 1 death strip: a resistance learned in Life 1 does not reach the Corridor (and Life 2).
tensura edit ability grant TtlBotWipe tensura:cold_resistance
ttl wipe TtlBotWipe expect has tensura:cold_resistance yes
kill TtlBotWipe
@sleep 1
ttl karma TtlBotWipe expect phase corridor
ttl wipe TtlBotWipe expect has tensura:cold_resistance no
ttl reset TtlBotWipe
ttlbot remove TtlBotWipe
